    "aurora.lead": "Norður doesn't say \"Kp 4, maybe\". It works out how visible the aurora would be where you are, right now.",
    "aurora.s1.title": "How much energy is coming in",
    "aurora.s1.text": "NOAA's OVATION model and the hemispheric power estimate the energy flux above you; the solar wind (speed, Bz) tells what will arrive in 30-60 minutes.",
    "aurora.s2.title": "How dark your sky is",
    "aurora.s2.text": "Twilight, the moon and the local light pollution brighten the sky: a faint aurora disappears in town and is clearly visible 20 km away.",
    "aurora.s3.title": "Whether clouds hide it",
    "aurora.s3.text": "Hour-by-hour cloud cover at your spot. The result is a clear verdict, with the solar wind's lead time to get ready.",
    "gallery.kicker": "Screens",
    "gallery.title": "Made to be read at a glance, even in the dark.",
    "honest.kicker": "Honesty",
    "honest.title": "What it does and what it doesn't",
    "honest.does": "What it does",
    "honest.doesnt": "What it doesn't",
    "honest.do": ["Brings the official sources together in one app: Veðurstofa Íslands, Vegagerðin, SafeTravel, NOAA, MET Norway and more.", "Alerts you even when the app is closed: aurora, weather warnings, closed roads, wind on your route.", "Works without signal with the last saved copy and the offline pack.", "Translates Icelandic notices into your language.", "Keeps your data on the phone: account and backup only if you want them."],
    "honest.dont": ["It doesn't replace official warnings: when in doubt, vedur.is, umferdin.is and 112 decide.", "It doesn't guarantee the aurora: nobody can. It tells you when the odds are good, and why.", "It doesn't book hotels, cars or tours and sells nothing.", "No ads, no data reselling.", "For now it's iPhone only."],
